 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-7710 (Renting and leasing of motor vehicles) motor-vehicle-rental-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-16"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607121000" "ADR-2607152500" "ADR-2607121200"]
 :mirrors "cloud-itonami-isic-7722 (vidrentalops.* module shape, Wave 4 human-facing-service class)"

 :context
 "ISIC Rev.4 7710 = renting and leasing of motor vehicles -- self-drive rental of
  cars, vans and light trucks to consumers and businesses (checkout/return desk
  operations, fleet-availability/maintenance scheduling, vehicle-safety-concern
  flagging, fleet procurement/replacement coordination). Live registry.edn :name
  for \"7710\" independently re-verified fresh via a clean clone: exact match
  \"Renting and leasing of motor vehicles\". A separate 3-digit group entry
  {:id \"771\"} with the same name (:repo nil, :maturity :spec) exists as a known
  redundant artifact of an earlier data-seeding pass -- left untouched.
  gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7710 confirmed a PRE-EXISTING
  repo already at :blueprint tier (CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md/CONTRIBUTING.md/
  GOVERNANCE.md/LICENSE/README.md/SECURITY.md/blueprint.edn/docs/ only, no
  deps.edn/src/test) -- this work ADDED the missing module set on top of that
  boilerplate, not a fresh scaffold. Motor-vehicle rental touches two Wave 4
  person-facing-service risk dimensions per ADR-2607152500: driver-eligibility
  decisions and vehicle-safety-clearance decisions -- closed op allowlist must
  never include an op that directly finalizes either; any 'flag concern' op
  always escalates, never auto-commit-eligible."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["finalizing a driver-eligibility override (waiving/overriding a driver-eligibility check to approve a renter) -- hard, permanent block"
  "finalizing a vehicle-safety-clearance decision (renting out a vehicle with a known mechanical defect) -- hard, permanent block"
  "payment capture/refund, contract negotiation, binding rental-agreement execution -- not represented in the closed op allowlist at all"]

 :self-trip-fix
 "Known fleet-wide bug class: bare-noun scope-excluded-terms (e.g. 'safety',
  'eligibility') self-match inside the mock advisor's own legitimate default
  rationale text, self-blocking the actor's happy path. Fix: scope-excluded-
  terms phrased as the finalization/execution ACTION ('finalize the driver-
  eligibility override', 'finalize the vehicle-safety clearance', JP
  equivalents), never a bare noun -- critical because :flag-vehicle-safety-
  concern's entire purpose is to discuss driver-eligibility/vehicle-safety
  topics using exactly those bare nouns. Dedicated regression test
  default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion in
  governor_test.clj asserts all 4 default proposal generators, for a clean
  registered+verified account, never trip :scope-excluded and never
  HARD-hold."

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-7710 with Store/Advisor/Governor/Phase/
  Operation/Sim, mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-7722's vidrentalops.* module
  shape module-for-module as vehiclerentalops.*:
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore, string-keyed accounts directory
    (account-id/name/registered?/verified?, a rental-desk/branch operating
    account), append-only ledger + rental-log
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + mock-advisor, 4 ops all :effect :propose --
    log-rental-record, schedule-fleet-operation, flag-vehicle-safety-concern,
    coordinate-fleet-restock
  - Governor (VehicleRentalGovernor): 2 named HARD checks (account-unverified,
    effect-not-propose) + scope-exclusion/op-not-allowed folded check
    (finalize-driver-eligibility-override / finalize-vehicle-safety-clearance /
    closed 4-op allowlist). always-escalate-ops #{:flag-vehicle-safety-concern},
    confidence-floor 0.6
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout (phase1 = log-rental-record only, approval; phase2 +=
    schedule-fleet-operation/coordinate-fleet-restock, approval; phase3
    auto-commits those 3 when clean+confident; flag-vehicle-safety-concern
    never auto, any phase)
  - Operation: real langgraph-clj StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->decide
    ->commit|hold|request-approval), interrupt-before #{:request-approval},
    NOT a stub -- mirrors vidrentalops.operation exactly
  - Sim: clojure -M:run demo, full happy path + always-escalate flow + all
    HARD-hold scenarios
  - Tests: store_contract_test, advisor_test, governor_test (incl. mandatory
    self-trip regression), phase_test, governor_contract_test -- 40 tests /
    119 assertions green
  - All .cljc portable, no JVM-only interop. AGPL-3.0-or-later. Pre-existing
    README/GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY/CODE_OF_CONDUCT boilerplate kept
    as-is, not recreated"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["ISIC 7710 motor-vehicle-rental-operations-coordination genuinely implemented
    and fully tested, filling in a pre-existing blueprint-tier repo"
   "driver-eligibility-override and vehicle-safety-clearance exclusions hardcoded
    in governor checks (scope-exclusion-violations), not just README prose"
   "self-trip bug class fixed by construction (action-phrased terms) + covered
    by dedicated regression test, not avoided by luck"
   "flag-vehicle-safety-concern always-escalate is a two-layer invariant (governor
    always-escalate-ops + phase's permanent absence from every :auto set)"
   "portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs; clojure -M:lint 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up; tests use
    in-memory MemStore, matching every sibling actor's current maturity"
   "mock-advisor is deterministic, not a real LLM call; Advisor protocol seam
    ready for that swap but not wired in this ADR"]}

